---
title: Company Information
description: Set up your company details, logo, and branding in FOSSBilling.
---

Enter your business details once so they appear consistently across invoices, emails, hosted pages, and client-facing documents.

## Where to Configure It

In the admin sidebar, go to **System → Settings**, select the **System** module, and open **Company Details**.

## Company Logo

Enter the address of your hosted image in **Logo URL**. For an alternate image for dark backgrounds, use **Logo URL (dark mode)**. See [logos in invoice PDFs](/admin-guide/invoice-pdf/#logos-and-remote-assets) for supported formats and size limits.

### Logo Not Showing?

Open the logo URL in your browser to check that the image loads. If the old logo still appears, [clear the application cache](/maintenance/troubleshooting/#clearing-the-cache) and your browser cache.

## Other Company Details

Configure the rest of your business profile in the same area:

| Setting | Where It Appears |
|---------|------------------|
| Company name | Invoices, emails, PDFs, client area |
| Address | Invoice PDFs, company profile |
| Email | System emails, contact forms |
| Phone | Client area, invoices |
| VAT/Tax ID | Invoice PDFs, tax calculations |
| Terms of Service | Checkout page, client agreements |

## Signatures

- For the company signature, fill in **Signature** under **Company Details**. The default [invoice PDF](/admin-guide/invoice-pdf/) uses it in the footer.
- For the email signature, go to **System → Settings**, select **Email**, open **Email Settings**, and fill in **Email Signature**. This sets `guest.system_email.signature` in [email templates](/admin-guide/email-templates/). Leave the field blank to use the company signature.

## Currency Settings

Select **Currency** under **System → Settings** to set the default currency, price format, and exchange rate sources.

See [Currency Support](/support/features/#currency-support) for more.
